# Cloudflare Workers static assets read this file from the assets directory
# (`next build` copies public/ into out/ verbatim) and apply the rules to
# every response. `#` lines are comments.
#
# No Content-Security-Policy, on purpose: a `next build` static export ships
# inline hydration scripts and inline <style> blocks, so a CSP here would
# need 'unsafe-inline' for both script-src and style-src — a header that
# reads as a defence and is nearly none — or per-page nonces, which a static
# export cannot issue. Better no CSP than a false one. Revisit this when the
# site leaves static export (the vinext follow-up); a middleware-injected
# CSP becomes possible then.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
